From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ncm_device: NTB parameters in RAM, and an out divisor Windows takes.

The ESP32-P4's USB controller reads a control transfer's data by DMA,
which can't reach the flash a const table lives in, so the host read
zeros for GET_NTB_PARAMETERS and Windows' NCM driver refused to start.

Windows' NCM driver (UsbNcm) also refuses an out divisor of 1 or 2 and
reports the device as failed (Code 10) right after reading the table.
It starts on 4 or 8; Linux' cdc_ncm takes any of them.

---
diff --git a/src/class/net/ncm_device.c b/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
--- a/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
+++ b/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
@@ -166,7 +166,8 @@
  * \attention
  *     We are lucky, that byte order is correct
  */
-TU_ATTR_ALIGNED(4) static const ntb_parameters_t ntb_parameters = {
+// In RAM: the USB controller reads control data by DMA, which can't reach flash.
+TU_ATTR_ALIGNED(4) static ntb_parameters_t ntb_parameters = {
   .wLength                  = sizeof(ntb_parameters_t),
   .bmNtbFormatsSupported    = 0x01,// 16-bit NTB supported
   .dwNtbInMaxSize           = CFG_TUD_NCM_IN_NTB_MAX_SIZE,
@@ -175,7 +176,9 @@
   .wNdbInAlignment          = TUD_NCM_ALIGNMENT,
   .wReserved                = 0,
   .dwNtbOutMaxSize          = CFG_TUD_NCM_OUT_NTB_MAX_SIZE,
-  .wNdbOutDivisor           = 1,
+  // Windows' NCM driver won't start on an out divisor of 1 or 2: it takes
+  // 4 or 8.
+  .wNdbOutDivisor           = 4,
   .wNdbOutPayloadRemainder  = 0,
   .wNdbOutAlignment         = TUD_NCM_ALIGNMENT,
   .wNtbOutMaxDatagrams      = CFG_TUD_NCM_OUT_MAX_DATAGRAMS_PER_NTB,
